rocedure might run on, and copy 2 runs on x2, so intervening on my node x1 doesn't shift the other copy's decision.\n\nI'm weighing the other copy's node against my own, and it turns out that under A-FDT the observations select different nodes, so the other copy keeps its prior. Under a do on my node alone, sending the letter dominates, so the procedure says defect regardless of q, and the fixed point has both defecting. The essay's own treatment of different-input copies as separate points the same way, so I'll submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9866,"completion_tokens":654,"total_tokens":10520,"cost":0.052544,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.052544,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039464,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01308},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":560,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}